 "title": "Recorder | SalineCountyMO",
 "text": "-->\nRecorder | SalineCountyMO\ntop of page\nHOME\nElected Offices\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCircuit Clerk\nCollector\nCommission\nCoroner\nCounty Clerk\nProsecuting Attorney\nPublic Administrator\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nCounty Departments\nBuilding and Grounds\nEmergency Management Agency\nHuman Resources\nRoad and Bridge\nElections\nAbout Us\nMore\nCounty Links\nDirectory\nHistorical Preservation\nPrevious Office Holders\nQ & A\nVeterans Memory Walk of Honor\nJessica L. Baker\n​\nHours:\nMonday through Friday\n8:00 am to 4:30 pm\n​\nLocation:\nSaline County Courthouse\n19 E. Arrow Street\nRoom 206\nMarshall, MO 65340\n​\nPhone:\n(660) 886-2677\n​\nFax:\n(660) 831-0649\n​\nEmail:\nrecorder@ salinecountymo.gov\nMeet the Recorder\nTo apply for a marriage license, please call the Recorder's office for an appointment at 660-886-2677\nThe Saline County Recorder of Deeds office is a county-elected position with a four year term. Jessica L. Baker has served as the Saline County Recorder since 2023. Other members of the team include:\nCarrie Jarvis- Chief Deputy, cjarvis@salinecountymo.gov\nKristin Bergstrom- Deputy, kbergstrom@salinecountymo.gov\nThe primary responsibility of the Recorder of Deeds office is making permanent records of Saline County real estate transactions, Federal and State tax liens, plats and surveys, military discharges and issuing marriage licenses.\nThe Saline County Recorder's Office offers two options for online land record searching.\n1) Tapestry: for the occasional user, 24/7 access, credit card based for payment as you go. Go to www.landrecords.com and select Saline County, Missouri.\n2) Laredo: monthly subscription option for frequent searching with 24/7 access. To subscribe, contact Jessica in the Recorder's office at 660-886-2677 or recorder@salinecountymo.gov .\nOnline land records date back to 1958, with older records being added daily. In-office records date back to 1821.\n﻿\nThe following link may be used to search marriage records in Saline County:\nhttps://mosaline.fidlar.com/MOSaline/Apex.WebPortal/Search\nOnline marriage records date back to 1970, and in-office records date back to the early 1800s. If you need a copy/certified copy of your marriage license, please contact our office.\n​\nSaline County now offers a free online subscription service, Property Fraud Alert, that allows individuals to have their name monitored within the County Recorder's office in order to track possible fraudulent recordings that affect their property. PFA is available in both English and Spanish. Alerts are sent via email, automated phone call, or text message. Alerts are sent within 24 hours after the document has been recorded. To sign up for this program, click the \"Property Fraud Alert\" button below, or call our office at 660-886-2677.\nFor any other questions, please contact our office at\n660-886-2677\n﻿Recorder@salinecountymo.gov\n﻿- Jessica L. Baker\n﻿Saline County Recorder of Deeds\nCarrie Jarvis\nChief Deputy\nKristin Bergstrom\nDeputy\nMarriage License Information\nInformation regarding obtaining a marriage license\nMarriage License Application\nBegin the marriage license application process\nDocument Requirements\nFind information regarding document requirements for recording\nFee Schedule\nBasic fees for the Recorder's Office\nOfficial Records Online\nOrder certified and uncertified marriage records\nProperty Fraud Alert\nProperty Fraud Alert is a free notification service offered to property owners in Saline County\nMarriage License Search\nSearch for online Saline County marriage records back to 1970\n﻿﻿© 2026 by Saline County Commission. All rights reserved.\nbottom of page",
